    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d689">

                <pb facs="0829" n="755" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg755"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/786</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-08-30T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 30, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 31, 2.15
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>697. My 672.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d689-f1"/> Axelrod, leader of Internationalist
                    section of Mensheviki and one of the Russian leaders of the Stockholm
                    Socialists’ Conference, has said in part: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>America is endangering future of humane culture by preventing peace. If
                            the President does not permit American delegates come to Stockholm he
                            will indicate that his country is more reactionary than despotic
                            Germany.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
